The desktop media list and the desktop capturer start, list and capture only with a
capturer WebRTC made, as the C++ wrapper's do (patches/wrapper/0007): WebRTC makes none
where it cannot capture that kind of source, and the list started the missing one on its
own thread and the capturer handed it to the cursor composer, which ended the program.
RTCDesktopCapturer's startCapture and startCaptureWithFPS: answer whether the capture
started, and its delegate hears that it did only once it has (startCapture told it before).

